Copied Blender source
---------------------
Two files carry Blender code (five upstream sources). The rule for any other: keep the
original copyright header on every file, add an entry here naming the file, the
upstream commit and the licence, and do not use the Blender or Cycles
trademarks to imply endorsement. docs/LICENSING.md has the
component-by-component table.

cpp/src/fe_polyfill.cpp
  Ported from  source/blender/blenlib/intern/polyfill_2d.cc
               source/blender/blenlib/intern/polyfill_2d_beautify.cc
  Upstream     blender/blender @ e240930f046045145f0e03ba237caa7192ccf449
  Copyright    2023 Blender Authors
  Licence      GPL-2.0-or-later (this repository distributes it under
               GPL-3.0-or-later, which the "or later" clause permits)
  What         the ear-clipping triangulator behind Blender's Triangulate
               modifier, and the BLI_polyfill_calc entry point; plus the
               beauty pass from polyfill_2d_beautify.cc -
               BLI_polyfill_beautify_quad_rotate_calc_ex, its half-edge
               rotation and edge-crease test - which is what the Triangulate
               modifier's "Beauty" method (the default) now runs. The KD-tree
               and BLI_heap live in BLI_ghash / BLI_edgehash upstream and are
               replaced by an open-addressing table here; the file's own header
               comment says what replaced them and why.

cpp/src/fe_modifiers.cpp - fe_mod_decimate_collapse()
  Ported from  source/blender/bmesh/tools/bmesh_decimate_collapse.cc
  Upstream     blender/blender @ e240930f046045145f0e03ba237caa7192ccf449
  Copyright    2023 Blender Authors
  Licence      GPL-2.0-or-later (this repository distributes it under
               GPL-3.0-or-later, which the "or later" clause permits)
  What         the edge-collapse decimator behind Blender's Decimate modifier:
               bm_decim_build_quadrics (face planes plus
               BOUNDARY_PRESERVE_WEIGHT = 100 boundary planes),
               bm_decim_calc_target_co_db (BLI_quadric_optimize with
               OPTIMIZE_EPS, midpoint fallback), bm_decim_build_edge_cost_single
               (|q1 + q2| evaluated at the target, COST_INVALID for edges that
               cannot collapse yet), bm_edge_collapse_is_degenerate_topology
               (the link condition) and bm_edge_collapse_is_degenerate_flip.
               Not ported: BMesh custom-data interpolation (vertex groups, shape
               keys, UV corners), the USE_SYMMETRY KD-tree pass and Blender's
               dissolve-based mode. The kernel works on a flat triangle buffer,
               so BMesh itself is not linked.

